{
  "format": "frontier-bend-ai",
  "version": 1,
  "summary": "How an element bot picks its next move (NpcBending; Tidebreak, the ring sport: the owner, 2026-10-04, the bots cast the same moves as the player). Every (move, mode) of its element's keys (Bending.keys) plus Mend and Patch is an option; each is scored every think by its role (offence, control, defence, mobility, reaction, sustain, setup), the element's personality, its range band and its 'when' (the need it answers), then a little chance (the bot's own seeded rng). Lock times are the player's own (SwayCaster's rule: the move's lock_s or mode_lock_s x the expert tier's mastery.lock_mult x the preset's lock_mult; a move's ai_factor only on easy and normal). Every number here is tuned by eye.",
  "_doc": {
    "defaults": "By the spec's do (the move's mode in data/sway/moves.json): role, range_m [near, far] (a number past 1 is metres; 'spec' takes the spec's own range_m or radius_m), cool_s (how long before it picks the same option again). An unknown do (a new one, 'throw') is treated as 'bolt'.",
    "zones": "A zone's role by its kind (spec.zone): the guards answer what flies at it (answers: attack kinds), the barriers are defence, the ground and the moving ones control.",
    "moves": "Per move, then per mode: what overrides the defaults (role, range_m, when, answers, cool_s, weight, combo {after: 'move/mode', bonus}). when: hurt (struck within hurt_s, or under half health), close (the foe within close_m), far (past far_m), stone_near (a stone on the line to the foe, or one it holds), own_wall (one of its walls up), own_damaged_wall, water_low, near_pool, rooted, slowed, foe_rooted, foe_airborne, room_back (room behind it), ice_near, foe_far.",
    "old": "The Sway's old spells (no bend spec: stone_form spike and cannonball, earth_wall wall, pillar self and free, gust push, pull and lift, mend): BendCast.cast casts them when it is there; without it only spike, wall and gust push are cast (NpcBending's own fallbacks).",
    "elements": "Each element's personality: a multiplier per role (and 'knock' for options whose knock_mps is 8 or more), react (x the preset's react_chance: how often a threat is answered at all; the soak 2026-10-05: air cushioned and shielded nearly every stone and bolt), and the range band it keeps between casts (keep_m).",
    "presets": "The difficulty: reaction_s (from a threat seen to its answer begun), scatter_deg (one sigma of the aim's line), lead (the share of a moving foe's lead taken), lock_mult (x the player's lock), ai_factor (the move's ai_factor applied: easy and normal only), react_chance (a threat answered at all), rest_s (between one release and the next lock), think_s, grace_s (the opening: from the round's start, or its making, no attack or control begun and nothing that knocks; guards and footwork only)."
  },
